# Security headers for static hosts that read a `_headers` file (Cloudflare
# Pages, Netlify, and similar). The exported HTML carries a meta CSP, but a meta
# policy cannot express `frame-ancestors`, and response headers like nosniff or
# a referrer policy are not something the app itself can set. Hosts that do not
# understand this file simply serve it as a static asset, so nothing depends on
# a particular host.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
